# Netlify header rules. This app has no build step and no hashed filenames --
# every JS/CSS file keeps the same URL forever -- so without this, a
# returning visitor's browser can silently keep running yesterday's code
# after a deploy, until they happen to hard-refresh. `no-cache` doesn't mean
# "never cache": it means always revalidate with the server first (a cheap
# conditional request), so an unchanged file still loads from cache but a
# changed one is never served stale.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
